// Title: PsExec Service Execution
// Sigma ID: fdfcbd78-48f1-4a4b-90ac-d82241e368c5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Thomas Patzke, Romaissa Adjailia, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2017-06-12 | Modified: 2023-02-28
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects launch of the PSEXESVC service, which means that this system was the target of a psexec
//   remote execution
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative tasks
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/sysinternals/downloads/psexec
//   - https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ro2QuZTIMBM
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_sysinternals_psexesvc.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\PSEXESVC.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "psexesvc.exe"
